Firstly, thank you for submitting your proposal for DevConf 2026. I’ve received ‘decline’ mails on many occasions, so please know that I understand how much it sucks. I hope this feedback offers some perspective and that my experience will help. The DevConf process is documented here <a href="https://www.devconf.co.za/selection" target="_blank">https://www.devconf.co.za/selection</a>, and it’s worth a read to put this feedback into context.

Just a note, that I am using a template to help write this feedback - there are so many requests, that using a template does help me respond to everyone so much faster. Please know that regardless of this template, I am reading everything in your submission and making sure you get personal content from me below. Also, this message has no AI helping me, it is just a template and my bad spelling. Candice may also respond if she thinks I omitted anything or got anything wrong.
2025 Stats:

💠 Number of submissions: 439
💠 Agenda capacity: 35. We reserve 5 slots for sponsors, which if not taken will be given back to the community. DevConf 2026 is also the first year we have 3 slots reserved for the top rated talks from 2025. This means we have 27 slots available; approx 6% of all submissions.
💠 Reviewers: 30 (including Candice and myself)
💠 Geography of submitters: 40% South African
💠    Geography of accepted speakers: 86% local to South Africa

Submissions that ranked highly were those that were well-written and:

💠 Positioned and described a problem/opportunity in some useful context, and to whom it would matter
💠 Included unique or novel insights
💠 Summarised at a high level the structure and/or contents of the talk
💠 Had locally specific relevance

